{"schemaVersion":1,"durationMinutes":30,"audioUrl":"","parts":[{"id":"en-c20-t2-l-p1","title":"Part 1","part_number":1,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/1714876-cambridge-ielts-20-academic-listening-2-audio1.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c20-t2-l-g1-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 1-10","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p><strong>Complete the notes below.</strong></p><p>Write&nbsp;<strong>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</strong>&nbsp;for each answer.</p><p>Local Councils can Arrange Practical Support to Help those Caring for Elderly people at Home.<strong></strong></p><strong></strong><p><strong></strong>This can give the carer:</p><p>– time for other responsibilities</p><p>–&nbsp; a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">1</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c20-t2-l-q1\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p><strong>Assessment of mother’s needs</strong></p><strong></strong><p><strong></strong>This may include discussion of:</p><p>– how much <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">2</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c20-t2-l-q2\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> the caring involves</p><p>What types of tasks are involved, e.g.:</p><p>– help with dressing</p><p>– helping her have a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">3</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c20-t2-l-q3\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>– shopping</p><p>– helping with meals</p><p>– dealing with <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">4</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c20-t2-l-q4\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>Any aspects of caring that are especially difficult, e.g.:<strong></strong></p><strong></strong><p><strong></strong>– loss of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">5</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c20-t2-l-q5\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>– <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">6</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c20-t2-l-q6\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> her</p><p>– preventing a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">7</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c20-t2-l-q7\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p><strong>Types of support that may be offered to carers</strong></p><p>– transport costs, e.g. cost of a&nbsp;<span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">8</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c20-t2-l-q8\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>– car-related costs, e.g. fuel and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">9</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c20-t2-l-q9\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>– help with housework</p><p>– help to reduce <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">10</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c20-t2-l-q10\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/cambridge-ielts-20-academic-listening-2-audio1.mp3"],"order_index":1},{"id":"en-c20-t2-l-p2","title":"Part 2","part_number":2,"passage